body:
* Start Date: 2018-02-05

# Summary

A connector for third-party integrations which doesn't have any rendering to set options for the InstantSearch instance. These options are sent on every `search` or `searchForFacetValues`.

# Motivation

Having `searchParameters` in `instantsearch()` makes sense for a static configuration, but as soon as you want to make it dynamic, it makes more sense as a widget, than as a parameter for InstantSearch. The main reason being that a widget is easier to change than a parameter on InstantSearch, and will be more consistent

# Detailed design

```js
const widgetFactory = connectConfigure(
 (state, isFirstRendering) => {
   // render nothing
 },
 () => {
   // just a necessary noop
 }
);

const widget = widgetFactory({
 analytics: true,
 ruleContexts: ["fancy context", "add dogs"]
});

search.addWidget(widget);

// later, if you want to change something:
const newWidget = widgetFactory({
 analytics: true,
 ruleContexts: ["boring context", "add dogs"]
});
search.addWidget(newWidget);
search.removeWidget(widget);
```

# How We Teach This

Add new entry in docs, implement in Vue InstantSearch and Angular InstantSearch as a widget.

# Drawbacks

This connector doesn't need a widget which renders anything, although in some cases it *could* make sense as a widget which is reconstructed if the parameters change, as a fallback just on top of a real custom widget. We should not take that usecase too much in account, but rather encourage custom widgets for that use case

# Alternatives

Use the helper directly in the libraries, but this is complicated as that would make components inconsistent

# Unresolved questions

* What happens on unmount
* What happens on conflicting parameters
